<DocsLayout
  title="MCP"
  subtitle="How nikcli connects local and remote Model Context Protocol servers, authenticates OAuth servers, and exposes MCP tools to agent sessions."
  description="Guide to configuring local and remote MCP servers, OAuth authentication, and MCP tool exposure."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      MCP support is implemented in <code>packages/nikcli/src/mcp/index.ts</code>. The service reads
      <code>config.mcp</code>, creates local stdio or remote HTTP/SSE clients, records status,
      converts server tools into AI SDK dynamic tools, and exposes prompts/resources to sessions.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
      <DocCard title="Local" eyebrow="stdio">
        <p>Runs a command in the current instance directory with environment from the config entry.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Remote" eyebrow="HTTP">
        <p>Tries Streamable HTTP first, then SSE, with optional headers and OAuth provider support.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="OAuth" eyebrow="Auth">
        <p>Stores tokens in <code>mcp-auth.json</code>, supports dynamic or configured client registration, and can open a browser for auth.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Tools" eyebrow="Agent">
        <p>MCP tool schemas are wrapped as strict dynamic tools with per-call timeout support.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="add-server" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Add a server</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>nikcli mcp add</code> for interactive config patching, or edit
      <code>mcp</code> in <code>nikcli.json</code> directly. <code>nikcli mcp list</code> initializes
      configured servers and shows status.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
nikcli mcp add
nikcli mcp list
nikcli mcp auth remote-docs
nikcli mcp auth list
nikcli mcp logout remote-docs
nikcli mcp debug remote-docs
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>mcp list</code></td><td>Read config, connect servers, show connected/disabled/failed/auth status.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp add</code></td><td>Add a local or remote MCP entry to global or project config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp auth</code></td><td>Start OAuth flow for a remote server with OAuth enabled.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp auth list</code></td><td>List OAuth-capable servers and token status.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp logout</code></td><td>Remove stored MCP auth for a server.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp debug</code></td><td>Inspect a configured server with a raw MCP client.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="local" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Local stdio servers</h2>
    <p>
      Local servers use <code>StdioClientTransport</code>. The command runs with cwd set to the
      current project directory. The environment is <code>process.env</code> plus configured
      <code>environment</code>; when the command is <code>nikcli</code>, <code>BUN_BE_BUN=1</code>
      is added.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="nikcli.json">
&#123;
  "mcp": &#123;
    "filesystem": &#123;
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["bunx", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "."],
      "environment": &#123;
        "LOG_LEVEL": "info"
      &#125;,
      "timeout": 30000
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>type</code></td><td>Yes</td><td><code>local</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>command</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Command array. First item is executable, rest are args.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>environment</code></td><td>No</td><td>Extra environment variables passed to the child process.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>enabled</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>false</code> keeps the server disabled.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>timeout</code></td><td>No</td><td>Connect and tool-list timeout in milliseconds. Default is 30000.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="remote" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Remote servers</h2>
    <p>
      Remote servers use two transports in sequence. nikcli tries
      <code>StreamableHTTPClientTransport</code> first, then <code>SSEClientTransport</code>. Both
      receive configured headers and the OAuth auth provider when OAuth is enabled.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="remote MCP">
&#123;
  "mcp": &#123;
    "remote-docs": &#123;
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://example.com/mcp",
      "headers": &#123;
        "X-Workspace": "docs"
      &#125;,
      "timeout": 45000
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>type</code></td><td>Yes</td><td><code>remote</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>url</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Remote MCP endpoint URL.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>headers</code></td><td>No</td><td>Static request headers for connect and capability calls.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>oauth</code></td><td>No</td><td>OAuth config object, <code>false</code> to disable OAuth, or omitted to enable OAuth support.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>enabled</code></td><td>No</td><td>Disable without deleting config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>timeout</code></td><td>No</td><td>Connection and capability-list timeout in milliseconds.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="oauth" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>OAuth</h2>
    <p>
      Remote MCP OAuth is on by default unless <code>oauth</code> is <code>false</code>. The
      <code>McpOAuthProvider</code> supports configured client id, client secret, and scope. Tokens,
      client metadata, code verifier, OAuth state, and server URL are stored through
      <code>McpAuth.Service</code> in <code>Global.Path.data/mcp-auth.json</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="pre-registered client">
&#123;
  "mcp": &#123;
    "corp-docs": &#123;
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://mcp.example.com",
      "oauth": &#123;
        "clientId": "client-id",
        "clientSecret": "client-secret",
        "scope": "read write"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Client registration errors">
      <p>
        If a server returns an unauthorized error mentioning registration or client id, nikcli reports
        <code>needs_client_registration</code> and asks you to add <code>clientId</code> in config.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="status" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Status model</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>connected</code></td><td>Client connected and <code>listTools</code> succeeded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>disabled</code></td><td>Config entry has <code>enabled: false</code> or the server was disconnected.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>failed</code></td><td>Connection or initial tool-list failed. Error string is stored.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>needs_auth</code></td><td>Remote server returned unauthorized and OAuth can continue.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>needs_client_registration</code></td><td>Remote server requires configured OAuth client id.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The service keeps <code>status</code> and <code>clients</code> maps in instance state. When the
      instance shuts down, all MCP clients are closed and pending OAuth transports are cleared.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Tools, prompts, resources</h2>
    <p>
      Connected MCP servers can contribute tools, prompts, and resources. Tool input schemas are
      wrapped as strict JSON schemas with <code>additionalProperties: false</code>. Tool calls use
      <code>resetTimeoutOnProgress</code> so long calls can continue when the server sends progress.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Service method</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Tools</td><td><code>tools</code></td><td>Fetches tool lists from connected clients and converts each MCP tool into an AI SDK dynamic tool.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Prompts</td><td><code>prompts</code></td><td>Lists prompts and names them as <code>client:prompt</code> after sanitizing names.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resources</td><td><code>resources</code></td><td>Lists resources and attaches client name to each resource record.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Prompt read</td><td><code>getPrompt</code></td><td>Calls the selected client's prompt with optional string args.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resource read</td><td><code>readResource</code></td><td>Reads a resource URI from the selected client.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tool-list changed</td><td><code>mcp.tools.changed</code></td><td>Published when a server sends <code>ToolListChangedNotification</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="api" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>API routes</h2>
    <p>MCP has both classic Hono routes and typed HttpApi handlers.</p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>GET /mcp</code></td><td>Status map.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp</code></td><td>Add a server config and attempt connection.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp/:name/auth</code></td><td>Start OAuth and return authorization URL in typed API.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp/:name/auth/callback</code></td><td>Finish OAuth with authorization code.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp/:name/auth/authenticate</code></td><td>Run full CLI/TUI OAuth flow where supported.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DELETE /mcp/:name/auth</code></td><td>Remove stored auth.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp/:name/connect</code></td><td>Connect or reconnect a server.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp/:name/disconnect</code></td><td>Close client and mark disabled.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>POST /mcp/:name/toggle</code></td><td>Patch config enabled state and disconnect when disabling.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="bash">
curl http://127.0.0.1:4096/mcp

curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:4096/mcp/remote-docs/connect

curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:4096/mcp/remote-docs/toggle \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '&#123;"enabled":false&#125;'
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="timeouts" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Timeouts and headers</h2>
    <p>
      The default MCP timeout is 30000 ms. A server-specific <code>timeout</code> overrides connect,
      initial <code>listTools</code>, and tool-call timeouts. Remote <code>headers</code> are passed
      to both Streamable HTTP and SSE transports.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Timeout failures remove tool availability">
      <p>
        If a connected client later fails to list tools, the MCP service records the failure and that
        server's tools are not added to the agent tool set until it reconnects successfully.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-modes" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Failure modes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>needs_auth</code></td><td>Remote server requires OAuth and no valid token is stored.</td><td>Run <code>nikcli mcp auth &lt;name&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>needs_client_registration</code></td><td>Server does not support dynamic client registration.</td><td>Add <code>oauth.clientId</code>, and client secret if required.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Local server failed</td><td>Command missing, bad args, bad cwd, or server did not initialize before timeout.</td><td>Run the command manually from the project directory and increase timeout if needed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Connected but no tools</td><td><code>listTools</code> failed after connect.</td><td>Check server logs and tool-list response.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Browser did not open</td><td>Automatic browser open failed.</td><td>The CLI prints the auth URL through the <code>mcp.browser.open.failed</code> event path.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="source-anchors" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Source anchors</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>File</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>MCP service</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/mcp/index.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>MCP auth storage</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/mcp/auth.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>OAuth provider and callback</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/mcp/oauth-provider.ts</code>, <code>packages/nikcli/src/mcp/oauth-callback.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>CLI command</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/mcp.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Classic routes</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/server/routes/mcp.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Typed routes</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/server/httpapi/mcp.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>TUI dialog</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/tui/component/dialog-mcp.tsx</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
